ight to  release the documents with the caveats  that they included in their release that  the information itself has not been  verified but that this is a document  about which briefings have taken place  at the highest  if you're against this release but not  against the countless releases of all  the Clinton email stuff and everything  else I mentioned you are exhibiting a  double standard and I believe that this  will actually facilitate the  determination of how accurate the  information in those 35 pages is I think  the unfortunate thing is that Trump is  able to brush a lot of this stuff off  because I mean there's a lot of stuff  from this report that probably isn't  true he's probably not into urine for  example but then he's able to put that  in the same box as this idea that the  Trump transition team had or the Trump  campaign had connections with Russia  during the campaign that part is  probably likely to be true yeah I think  it's incredibly unlikely that no one on  the Trump team and no one from Russia oh  we're in touch during the campaign and  I've been saying that even before the  release of this document so I think  you're absolutely right Trump is sort of  conflating the entire thing mixing the  truth about the fact that there was a  briefing about this versus the truth of  the contents of it and then writing it  all off as fake news thanks for watching  this video before you watch the next one  remember we're raising money to expand  the David Pakman show big league as well  as expand progressive activism go to  david pakman.com slash donate donations  of any size are much appreciated
 

